<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icef34578ad2260f4b56ca1f9957a35daea4ce97a" commit="1e4a1e17f127208fd8d7285dc54c9ae651e2bb86" commit_message="platform_HWwatchdog: Separate watchdog control into helper class  This patch moves most of the logic from platform_HWwatchdog into a separate helper class so the code can be reused by other tests that need to interact with the hardware watchdog.  BUG=None TEST=Ran platform_HWwatchdog on Oak.  Change-Id: Icef34578ad2260f4b56ca1f9957a35daea4ce97a Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334743 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334743" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/43/334743/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie00e471b5cad5048ca76a1bf13b5f4d4b9946696" commit="95d3fbeb8491b6952c2643e67e1fe42419a078bd" commit_message="firmware_EventLog: Test for hardware watchdog event  This patch adds a check for the watchdog timeout event to the firmware_EventLog test. Skipping x86 devices for now which don't seem to report this event (at least on my old Falco).  Also change all the TestError in this test to TestFail which is actually the correct exception to throw for cases where the board doesn't meet expectations (as opposed to cases where the test logic itself ran into an unexpected condition somehow).  BUG=None TEST=Ran on Oak.  Change-Id: Ie00e471b5cad5048ca76a1bf13b5f4d4b9946696 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334744 Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334744" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/44/334744/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7169cb218923680b7f03618b652d5627b88b038c" commit="546905327c8b2c670341ec4fa33a1a462a6d76e5" commit_message="Marking set of ebuilds as stable  Marking the following ebuilds as stable:  * chromeos-base/apmanager  * chromeos-base/attestation  * chromeos-base/chromeos-dbus-bindings  * chromeos-base/firewalld  * chromeos-base/libbrillo  * chromeos-base/shill  * chromeos-base/shill-client  * chromeos-base/shill-test-scripts  * chromeos-base/tpm_manager  * chromeos-base/trunks  * chromeos-base/update_engine  * chromeos-base/update_engine-client  * chromeos-base/webserver  Pulled 2 new changes from platform/system/connectivity/shill:   919aa73 Add ThirdPartyVpn suspend/resume events   642dd96 Handle VPN reconnections on link down/up/changed  Pulled 1 new changes from platform/system/tpm:   5b90435 trunks: Fix MIPS policy syscall names.  Pulled 1 new changes from platform/system/update_engine:   6e30bc5 Handle AllowKioskAppControlChromeVersion device policy  Pulled 1 new changes from chromiumos/platform2:   e5d02c2 crash: Label ARC crashes in chrome://crashes  BUG=chromium:577783 TEST=trybots  Change-Id: I7169cb218923680b7f03618b652d5627b88b038c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335665 Commit-Ready: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Xiyuan Xia &lt;xiyuan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335665" owner_email="deymo@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/65/335665/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iacc6b5809920ec91ca24458e83d1892052ca05f4" commit="85418eed48e45945ee5b1039aa6b1270c1bd0487" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/cirrus: implement hardware cursor support  This CL implements hardware support for cursors through cirrus DRM. It only supports ARGB 8-bit cursors from userspace, and downconverts them to 1-bit black and white with masking, which is all cirrus hardware can support. Only cursors with size 32x32 or 64x64 will work.  The intention of adding cursor support is to make it far easier to use Chromium OS in QEMU.  TEST=ui or drm_cursor_test in QEMU BUG=chromium:594885  (cherry picked from f60867c0c5dbd7271f4564b197876cbd71047468) Change-Id: Iacc6b5809920ec91ca24458e83d1892052ca05f4 Signed-off-by: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335579 Commit-Ready: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335579" owner_email="zachr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/79/335579/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6" commit="e5f28feb74288b542b4093562375aff9693517f2" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iwlwifi: mvm: add a scan timeout for regular scans  If something goes wrong with the firmware and we never get a scan complete notification, we stay stuck forever.  In order to avoid this situation, add a timeout and trigger an NMI if it expires before receiving the notification., so we can clean things up.  BUG=cheomeos-partner:48182, 50672, 49779, 50653 TEST=Keep rebooting the machine for about 6 hours and make sure that it can always connect  Change-Id: I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6 Signed-off-by: Luca Coelho &lt;luciano.coelho@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334633 Commit-Ready: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Sameer Nanda &lt;snanda@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334633" owner_email="luciano.coelho@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/33/334633/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idb4b495c363699e99d84bad1a251341f60aa5e77" commit="278f47facfd9bea73a5aa9550742b259f54d1150" commit_message="adb_host: Support running tests over TCP/IP  * Cleaned up the old unused TCP/IP logic. * Updated the adb_host to enable TCP/IP mode if the serial contains   a port. When this mode is enabled, test_droid instructs the test   station to adb connect to the device when resetting the adbd   connection.  BUG=chromium:598789 TEST=test_droid.py -s 192.168.86.113:5555 brillo_DiskSizeTest &amp;      test_droid.py -s 92c52320 brillo_DiskSizeTest  Change-Id: Idb4b495c363699e99d84bad1a251341f60aa5e77 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335683 Commit-Ready: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Pursell &lt;dpursell@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335683" owner_email="sbasi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/83/335683/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iedbfe63ead401c1391e80d5a481f050bc698044e" commit="00da91491ba0b809c8a36bb72001ce284652bf40" commit_message="drm-tests: make drm_cursor_test take cursor size as an argument  This CL makes drm_cursor_test take one optional parameter, which shall be the cursor size in pixels. The cursor is always square, so only one integer parameter is needed. Without parameters, the test behavior is unchanged.  I used this test for the cirrus hw cursor driver, which has radically different image formats for its different cursor sizes.  TEST=`drm_cursor_test 32` on cirrus on QEMU w/ CL:333709 BUG=chromium:594885  Change-Id: Iedbfe63ead401c1391e80d5a481f050bc698044e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335323 Commit-Ready: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335323" owner_email="zachr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/drm-tests" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/drm-tests" ref="refs/changes/23/335323/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1d44d93d328d9a6f4e1fd548b500a8ad5e1149a3" commit="88c292b917986083b7bee0f4c773da027faa276f" commit_message="Banon: Add to Strago based mainboard list for mosys  Add Banon mainboard to Strago board list for mosys.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=run &quot;emerge-banon mosys&quot;  Change-Id: I1d44d93d328d9a6f4e1fd548b500a8ad5e1149a3 Signed-off-by: David Wu &lt;David_Wu@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335528 Commit-Ready: David Wu &lt;david_wu@quantatw.com&gt; Tested-by: David Wu &lt;david_wu@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335528" owner_email="david_wu@quantatw.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/mosys" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/mosys" ref="refs/changes/28/335528/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6" commit="a8b40b375c03abce23d27a32ccb7e639bf77240d" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iwlwifi: mvm: add a scan timeout for regular scans  If something goes wrong with the firmware and we never get a scan complete notification, we stay stuck forever.  In order to avoid this situation, add a timeout and trigger an NMI if it expires before receiving the notification., so we can clean things up.  BUG=cheomeos-partner:48182, 50672, 49779, 50653 TEST=Keep rebooting the machine for about 6 hours and make sure that it can always connect  Change-Id: I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6 Signed-off-by: Luca Coelho &lt;luciano.coelho@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333755 Commit-Ready: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Sameer Nanda &lt;snanda@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="333755" owner_email="luciano.coelho@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/55/333755/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6" commit="7e69cae57f9b37fd0817665655951eacc16ded4e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iwlwifi: mvm: add a scan timeout for regular scans  If something goes wrong with the firmware and we never get a scan complete notification, we stay stuck forever.  In order to avoid this situation, add a timeout and trigger an NMI if it expires before receiving the notification., so we can clean things up.  BUG=cheomeos-partner:48182, 50672, 49779, 50653 TEST=Keep rebooting the machine for about 6 hours and make sure that it can always connect  Change-Id: I17d8c82fd9c08082e8a070fcc839c333e79d11a6 Signed-off-by: Luca Coelho &lt;luciano.coelho@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334673 Commit-Ready: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Sameer Nanda &lt;snanda@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334673" owner_email="luciano.coelho@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/73/334673/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ife99c817e45d5f2347f005d208805ea12eda515a" commit="d2b9ddf9ca3b7b014e0ee12535179b9861fa0b19" commit_message="Add libcontainer ebuild  Build and install the new libcontainer so that session manager can use it in a future change.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:323433 BUG=b/26549867 TEST=emerge-samus chromeos-libcontainer  Change-Id: Ife99c817e45d5f2347f005d208805ea12eda515a Signed-off-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323316 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323316" owner_email="dgreid@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/16/323316/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2d053b18ba624f4ce3ebc1956b9e7945b693b0bc" commit="28e811b5aec7f6da90f47aa1f2850bad11a95b37" commit_message="file: read in entire file (up to 4K) instead of stat()'ing for size  We use find_string() to check files in both /proc (e.g., /proc/device-tree/...) and /sys (e.g., /sys/bus/spi/devices/...). find_string() currently tries to iteratively read pieces of these files, using stat() to get the file size. However, this size is inaccurate on sysfs, as these files are often dynamically generated, so it reports a size of PAGE_SIZE (i.e., 4096).  Instead of trying to pre-determine the file size, let's read in the whole file (up to 4KiB - 1) and do a series of string searches to find any matching strings. The 4KiB limitation should be OK, since we're only looking for things like modalias and compatible strings.  As a side effect, this eliminates a lot of unnecessary strlen() calls, and allows us to again avoid hand-rolling strstr().  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51651 BRANCH=none TEST=`flashrom --wp-status` doesn't show log spam TEST=`flashrom --read /tmp/flashX` gives same results before/after  Change-Id: I2d053b18ba624f4ce3ebc1956b9e7945b693b0bc Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335353 Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335353" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/53/335353/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id847e1115a8a92db1e889d6de206a67982feaaf5" commit="94a7acc4d80d09cdedd41a22a2adf133df1a20e1" commit_message="labstation: Create project and variant overlay.  The project-labstation overlay is to support a test station and servo host. The overlay-variant-guado-labstation is the initial overlay to be used. Refactored the chromeos-test-testauthkeys ebuild into project-mobbase from project-moblab.  BUG=chromium:588368 TEST=Built image and flashed it on a guado and it booted up.  Still need to test that servo and test station capabilities are working.  Change-Id: Id847e1115a8a92db1e889d6de206a67982feaaf5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328774 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328774" owner_email="kevcheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="17" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/74/328774/17" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="8128.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>